PART 1. Fox calculus: dr/db at psi (a->t, b->1), versus X_0 cap N
==============================================================================

  m003: r = abAAbabbb, e_a(r)=0, e_b(r)=5
    precondition e_a(r)=0 (needed since lambda is not a root of unity): True
    dr/da at psi = 0   (fundamental identity forces 0 when e_a=0 and t != 1)
    dr/db at psi = (t**2 + 3*t + 1)/t
    roots t=lambda^2 of dr/db: [-3/2 - sqrt(5)/2, -3/2 + sqrt(5)/2]
    c^2 = t + 2 + 1/t from Fox roots: [-1]
    c^2 from X_0 cap N (independent Groebner/solve): [-1]
    MATCH: True
    primitive integer polynomial t**2 + 3*t + 1, leading coeff 1: monic
    monic; root moduli [2.61803398874989, 0.381966011250105] (roots of unity have modulus 1)

  m006: r = ababbAAbb, e_a(r)=0, e_b(r)=5
    precondition e_a(r)=0 (needed since lambda is not a root of unity): True
    dr/da at psi = 0   (fundamental identity forces 0 when e_a=0 and t != 1)
    dr/db at psi = 2*t**2 + t + 2
    roots t=lambda^2 of dr/db: [-1/4 - sqrt(15)*I/4, -1/4 + sqrt(15)*I/4]
    c^2 = t + 2 + 1/t from Fox roots: [3/2]
    c^2 from X_0 cap N (independent Groebner/solve): [3/2]
    MATCH: True
    primitive integer polynomial 2*t**2 + t + 2, leading coeff 2: NOT monic, so roots are not algebraic integers, hence not roots of unity

